    10	and official conformance environment is Node.js 22. `@mcpfn/core` and
    11	`@mcpfn/auth` additionally support web-standard edge runtimes such as Cloudflare
    12	Workers (see "Edge and Cloudflare Workers" below). The remaining top-level
    13	package entries are Node runtimes: stdio, cryptography, module loading, and
    14	local fixture tools are not advertised as browser or edge bundles. Desktop and
    15	native products may consume a remote Streamable HTTP target or run the Node
    16	client in a managed subprocess. No browser-specific export condition is provided
    17	in this release.
    18	
    19	The official MCP SDK is the only protocol, JSON-RPC, initialization, and
    20	transport implementation. McpFn adds application declarations, lifecycle
    21	ownership, OAuth compatibility policy, testing, artifacts, and inspection.
    22	
    23	## Edge and Cloudflare Workers
    24	
    25	`@mcpfn/core` and `@mcpfn/auth` ship self-contained bundles: the official MCP
    26	SDK and a single pinned Zod runtime are inlined into each package's `dist`
    27	output. A consumer can bundle either package for a Cloudflare Worker alongside
    28	its own root `zod` dependency without adding a bundler alias, an import
    29	condition override, or any other application-local shim. Inlining removes the
    30	"mixed Zod entry point" hazard in which a consumer's bundler would otherwise
    31	resolve the SDK's internal `zod/v4` import to a different physical Zod copy than
    32	the one the schemas were constructed against.
    33	
    34	Schema validation adapts to the host runtime. On Node the packages compile JSON
    35	Schema with Ajv. On runtimes that forbid runtime code generation (Cloudflare
    36	Workers reject `new Function`), the packages fall back to
    37	`@cfworker/json-schema`, which validates without code generation. Both engines
    38	normalize errors to the same shape, so protocol behavior and error envelopes are
    39	unchanged.
    40	
    41	`@mcpfn/client`, `@mcpfn/cli`, `@mcpfn/testing`, and `@mcpfn/inspector` remain
    42	Node-targeted. `@mcpfn/client` re-exports the stdio client transport, which
    43	depends on `child_process`; it is not offered as an edge bundle. Edge consumers
    44	serve MCP with `@mcpfn/core` and, when they need OAuth resource-server behavior,
    45	`@mcpfn/auth`.
    46	
    47	A representative Cloudflare Worker startup check is part of the guarded release.
    48	`npm run gate:mcpfn-release` bundles a worker that imports `@mcpfn/core` next to
    49	a root `zod`, boots it under the `workerd` runtime, and drives a real MCP client
    50	through `initialize`, `tools/list`, and `tools/call`. The check also asserts,
    51	from the bundler's module graph, that no external `zod/v4` or SDK entry leaks
    52	into the worker bundle.
    53	
    54	## Public format policy
    55	
    56	Manifests, scenario artifacts, scenario reports, target-suite reports, and
    57	client events use integer `formatVersion: 1`. Inspector snapshots use
    58	`formatVersion: 2`; version 2 removes the version 1 `state` field and replaces
    42	
    43	Set `clientRequirements` for roots, sampling, or elicitation used by handlers. Add extension declarations for MCP Apps, then check the manifest against the intended host profile in CI. This turns a host capability mismatch into a pre-release failure instead of a runtime surprise.
    44	
    45	## 8. Deploy to Cloudflare Workers or other edge runtimes
    46	
    47	`@mcpfn/core` and `@mcpfn/auth` are self-contained: the MCP SDK and a single
    48	pinned Zod runtime are inlined into their `dist` output. Bundle them into a
    49	Worker directly, even when your application also depends on a different root
    50	`zod` version. You do not need a bundler alias for `zod`/`zod/v4`, an import
    51	condition override, or any other application-local shim.
    52	
    53	Serve MCP over the Web Standard handler (Streamable HTTP) and wrap it with
    54	`@mcpfn/auth` when the endpoint is protected. Do not import `@mcpfn/client`,
    55	`@mcpfn/cli`, `@mcpfn/testing`, or `@mcpfn/inspector` from an edge bundle; those
    56	packages depend on Node-only capabilities such as the stdio transport's
    57	`child_process`. Tool and prompt schema validation switches to
    58	`@cfworker/json-schema` automatically on runtimes that forbid runtime code
    59	generation, so no configuration is required. The `cloudflare:worker-startup`
    60	step of `npm run gate:mcpfn-release` exercises this exact deployment shape under
    61	the `workerd` runtime.
    62	
    63	## Existing Superfunctions migrations
    64	
    65	LangFn, MemoryFn, and ProbeFn migrations are outside this release. Their existing
    66	MCP compatibility surfaces remain unchanged until each consumer is migrated and
    67	its own regression suite is added to the release gate.
    68	
   106	
   107	`createWebStandardHandler()` accepts the official SDK `HandleRequestOptions`, including validated `authInfo`. Use `@mcpfn/auth` to publish OAuth protected-resource metadata and produce that trusted value. In stateless mode, McpFn creates and disposes an isolated SDK server and transport for every request. Attach protocol instrumentation with `configureRequestServer`; it receives the live isolated server before transport connection and runs once per request, or once per session initialization attempt. Because configuration precedes SDK request validation, a rejected attempt can invoke the hook without retaining a session. Supply a cryptographically secure `sessionIdGenerator` when the server uses sampling, elicitation, or another server-to-client request that must be correlated across HTTP requests; session-enabled handlers retain their transport across the session.
   108	
   109	## Cloudflare Workers and edge runtimes
   110	
   111	`@mcpfn/core` is a self-contained bundle: the official MCP SDK and a single
   112	pinned Zod runtime are inlined into `dist`. Bundle it into a Cloudflare Worker
   113	next to your application's own root `zod` dependency without adding a bundler
   114	alias for `zod`/`zod/v4`, an import condition override, or any other
   115	application-local shim. Serve MCP through `createWebStandardHandler()`. Schema
   116	validation uses Ajv on Node and falls back to `@cfworker/json-schema` on
   117	runtimes that forbid runtime code generation, such as `workerd`, so no
   118	configuration is required. See
   119	[ADR-0001](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/main/mcpfn/ADR-0001-COMPATIBILITY.md)
   120	for the compatibility policy.
   121	
   122	See the [architecture](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/main/mcpfn/ARCHITECTURE.md), [testing guide](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/main/mcpfn/TESTING.md), and runnable [calculator example](https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/blob/main/mcpfn/examples/calculator-server.ts).

