<excerpt># File: cfworker/cfworker/packages/json-schema/README.md - Repository: cfworker/cfworker | A collection of packages optimized for Cloudflare Workers and service workers. | 681 stars | TypeScript - Branch: main ```md # `@cfworker/json-schema` ![](https://badgen.net/bundlephobia/minzip/@cfworker/json-schema) ![](https://badgen.net/bundlephobia/min/@cfworker/json-schema) ![](https://badgen.net/bundlephobia/dependency-count/@cfworker/json-schema) ![](https://badgen.net/bundlephobia/tree-shaking/@cfworker/json-schema) ![](https://badgen.net/npm/types/@cfworker/json-schema?icon=typescript) A JSON schema validator that will run on Cloudflare workers. Supports drafts 4, 7, 2019-09, and 2020-12. This library is validated against the [json-schema-test-suite](https://github.com/json-schema-org/JSON-Schema-Test-Suite), a series of approximately 4,500 assertions maintained along with the json-schema specification. A small set of test cases are intentionally not supported due to performance constraints or lack of feature use. These list of unsupported features are maintained in [test/unsupported.ts](./test/unsupported.ts). While this library is not the fastest due to lack of code generation, it&`#39`;s consistently among the [most spec compliant](https://json-schema.org/implementations.html#benchmarks). ## Background _Why another JSON schema validator?_ Cloudflare workers do not have APIs required by [Ajv](https://ajv.js.org/) schema compilation (`eval` or `new Function(code)`). If possible use Ajv in a build step to precompile your schema. Otherwise this library could work for you. ## Basic usage ```js import { Validator } from &`#39`;`@cfworker/json-schema`&`#39`;; const validator = new Validator({ type: &`#39`;number&`#39`; }); const result = validator.validate(7); ``` ## Specify meta schema draft ```js const validator = new Validator({ type: &`#39`;number&`#39`; }, &`#39`;4&`#39`;); // draft-4 ``` ## Add schemas ```js const validator = new Validator({ $id: &`#39`;https://foo.bar/baz&`#39`;, $ref: &`#39`;/beep&`#39`; }); validator.addSchema({ $id: &`#39`;https://foo.bar/beep&`#39`;, type: &`#39`;boolean&`#39`; }); ``` ## Include all errors By default the validator stops processing after the first error. Set the `shortCircuit` parameter to `false` to emit all errors. ```js const shortCircuit = false; const draft = &`#39`;2019-09&`#39`;; const schema = { type: &`#39`;object&`#39`;, required: [&`#39`;name&`#39`;, &`#39`;email&`#39`;, &`#39`;number&`#39`;, &`#39`;bool&`#39`;], properties: { name: { type: &`#39`;string&`#39`; }, email: { type: &`#39`;string&`#39`;, format: &`#39`;email&`#39`; }, number: { type: &`#39`;number&`#39`; }, bool: { type: &`#39`;boolean&`#39`; } } }; const validator = new Validator(schema, draft, shortCircuit); const result = validator.validate({ name: &`#39`;hello&`#39`;, email: 5, // invalid type number: &`#39`;Hello&`#39`; // invalid type bool: &`#39`;false&`#39`; // invalid type }); ``` ```</excerpt>
