<excerpt># v1.9.0 `@cfworker/json-schema/dist/validator.js` - Error when importing - State: closed - Author: pbeck6 - Created: 2021-11-13T05:34:52Z - Updated: 2021-11-20T14:31:02Z - Repository: cfworker/cfworker - Number: `#156` ## Labels - question --- The following code in validator.js: ``` export class Validator { schema; draft; shortCircuit; lookup; constructor(schema, draft = &`#39`;2019-09&`#39`;, shortCircuit = true) { this.schema = schema; this.draft = draft; this.shortCircuit = shortCircuit; this.lookup = dereference(schema); // rest of code } ``` causes a loader error when attempting to `import { Validator } from &`#39`;`@cfworker/json-schema`&`#39`;`. It appears JS does not understand `schema, draft, shortCircuit, lookup` public instance fields appearing before constructor. Issue is fixed after removing. Working validator.js code: ``` export class Validator { constructor(schema, draft = &`#39`;2019-09&`#39`;, shortCircuit = true) { this.schema = schema; this.draft = draft; this.shortCircuit = shortCircuit; this.lookup = dereference(schema); // rest of code } ``` ## Timeline **jdanyow** commented on 2021-11-14T04:12:25Z: &gt; Those are public instance fields. Where are you seeing the error? The 1.9.0 code runs in the browser/workers without any compilation. &gt; &gt; ```html &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; GistRun &gt; &gt; import { Validator } from &`#39`;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@cfworker/json-schema@1.9.0/dist/index.js&`#39`;; &gt; const validator = new Validator({ type: &`#39`;number&`#39`; }); &gt; let result = validator.validate(1); &gt; document.body.insertAdjacentHTML(&`#39`;beforeend&`#39`;, ` ${JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)} `); &gt; result = validator.validate(&`#39`;hello&`#39`;); &gt; document.body.insertAdjacentHTML(&`#39`;beforeend&`#39`;, ` ${JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)} `); &gt; &gt; &gt; &gt; Hello world! &gt; &gt; &gt; ``` &gt; https://gist.run/?id=a4f6c9b5854d10bcfe9c39f7345bcd10 - jdanyow added label &quot;question&quot; **pbeck6** 