4\. Release gate lacks direct dependencies <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>☼ Reliability</code>

<pre>
The new Worker gate imports <b><i>esbuild</i></b>, <b><i>miniflare</i></b>, and the MCP SDK directly even though the root
manifest does not declare any of them. The gate currently relies on npm hoisting them from workspace
or Cloudflare-pool transitive dependencies, so a dependency-layout change can make the release gate
fail with module-resolution errors or run against an unintended SDK version.
</pre>


<details>
<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>

```
## Issue description
The new root-level release-gate script directly imports packages that are absent from the root package manifest. Its execution therefore depends on incidental transitive hoisting rather than an explicit root dependency contract.

## Fix Focus Areas
- scripts/test-mcpfn-cloudflare-worker.mjs[18-25]
- package.json[131-145]
- package-lock.json[22050-22055]

## Recommended Fix
Add `esbuild`, `miniflare`, and the intended `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` version to the root `devDependencies`, then regenerate the lockfile with the repository's supported npm version. Keep the script imports aligned with those declared root dependencies so clean and future installations run the gate deterministically.
```

