```
## Issue description
`compileSchema()` reuses a module-global Ajv instance, so schemas from independent `McpFnRegistry` instances and separate manifest validations share Ajv's `$id` registry. Valid schemas that reuse an identifier therefore fail after another schema has already been compiled.

## Fix Focus Areas
- mcpfn/core/src/validation.ts[40-49]
- mcpfn/core/src/validation.ts[90-112]
- mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts[372-439]
- mcpfn/core/src/manifest.ts[209-231]

## Recommended Fix
Replace the module-global Ajv compiler with compiler instances scoped to the former validation boundaries: one per `McpFnRegistry` and one per `validateManifest()` call. Expose a factory for runtime-appropriate schema compilers if needed, retain the cfworker fallback behavior, and add regression coverage proving that two independent registries and sequential manifest validations can use distinct schemas with the same `$id`.
```

